        "v": 5,
        "title": "Filter malformed paths in getFileVersionUpdates",
        "summary": "Added path validation filter to `getFileVersionUpdates` in `backend/src/main-prompt.ts`. Paths containing `..` or causing `path.normalize` exceptions are now excluded before `requestFiles` execution. This prevents server errors from malformed file path inputs.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T18:28:18.506Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "The server now quietly skips any file paths that look broken or suspicious (ones containing '..' or that would cause an error) before it tries to fetch those files, so these bad paths no longer crash the feature that updates your recent file lists. If you tried to trigger it with a malformed path, the request would have thrown an error previously; instead, the system will now just ignore those problematic entries. This is live today in the backend.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
