        "v": 5,
        "title": "Per-user referral limits replace global MAXREFERRALS constant",
        "summary": "Referral caps now enforce per-user limits via new `referral_limit` integer column in `user` table, replacing global `MAX_REFERRALS` constant. Migration `0006_first_quasimodo.sql` adds column with default 5 NOT NULL. `hasMaxedReferrals` checks user-specific limit from DB instead of constant. Web API returns `referralLimit` number instead of `limitReached` boolean.",
        "significance": "notable",
        "at": "2026-09-15T18:27:12.628Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "Previously, there was a single global cap on how many people any one user could refer. That cap has been replaced with a personal limit stored on each user's account, so each person's allowance can be set individually instead of everyone sharing one number. If you looked, your profile now carries its own referral allowance and the system checks that number rather than a shared constant; the referral page now reports how much room you have left instead of just saying you're blocked.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
        "v": 4,
