        "v": 5,
        "title": "Filter absolute paths in file version updates",
        "summary": "Backend file version update logic now filters out absolute paths before processing. This prevents path traversal or normalization issues when handling requested, previous, and edited file paths in `backend/src/main-prompt.ts`. The `request-files-prompt.ts` instructions were also updated to explicitly require \"full relative path\" instead of just \"full path\". These changes harden path handling in the backend.",
        "significance": "minor",
        "at": "2026-09-15T18:26:34.544Z"
      },
      "eli5": {
        "text": "When the system keeps track of which files have been requested or edited, it now rejects any file location given as an absolute path (one that starts from the root of the drive). This keeps the system from accidentally reading or writing files outside the project folder it should be working in. You wouldn't see this unless you were watching the backend logs for rejected paths, but it makes file handling safer and more predictable.",
        "model": "vyce/deepseek-v4.1",
